      "text": "To evaluate \\(\\log_3 27\\sqrt{3}\\), we first express \\(27\\sqrt{3}\\) as a power of 3. We know that:\n\n\\[27 = 3^3\\]\n\\[\\sqrt{3} = 3^{1/2}\\]\n\nTherefore,\n\n\\[27\\sqrt{3} = 3^3 \\cdot 3^{1/2} = 3^{3 + 1/2} = 3^{7/2}\\]\n\nNow we need to find \\(\\log_3 3^{7/2}\\). By the properties of logarithms, specifically the change of base formula \\(\\log_b a = \\frac{\\log_c a}{\\log_c b}\\), we can use the fact that \\(\\log_3 3 = 1\\) and \\(\\log_3 3^{7/2} = \\frac{\\log_3 3^{7/2}}{\\log_3 3} = \\frac{7/2}{1} = \\frac{7}{2}\\).\n\nThus, the value of \\(\\log_3 27\\sqrt{3}\\) is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{7}{2}}\\).",
