      "text": "First, we rewrite the expression as $\\log_3 (27 \\cdot \\sqrt{3})$.\nNext, we simplify the expression inside the logarithm by using the property $\\log_b (mn) = \\log_b m + \\log_b n$.\nSo, $\\log_3 (27 \\cdot \\sqrt{3}) = \\log_3 27 + \\log_3 \\sqrt{3}$.\nWe can further simplify $\\log_3 27$ by recognizing that $27 = 3^3$, so $\\log_3 27 = \\log_3 3^3 = 3$.\nSimilarly, $\\log_3 \\sqrt{3}$ can be simplified by recognizing that $\\sqrt{3} = 3^{1/2}$, so $\\log_3 \\sqrt{3} = \\log_3 3^{1/2} = \\frac{1}{2}$.\nPutting it all together, we have $\\log_3 (27 \\cdot \\sqrt{3}) = \\log_3 27 + \\log_3 \\sqrt{3} = 3 + \\frac{1}{2} = \\boxed{\\frac{7}{2}}$.The answer is: \\frac{7}{2}",
